description:
Objective: give the protected guest supervisor (scripts/local-runner/guest-supervisor.py) a root, copy-only 'agents' mode. It installs the pinned agent CLI binaries the host streams on stdin at /opt/moe/agents/<cli>, root:root 0555 and never agent-writable, and it never leaves a partial install.

This is the guest half of CQ-R10d3 (task-b8e7ad92), split off on 2026-10-30 by architect-bd1eb82d so that each slice stays under QA's 400-line cap. CQ-R10d3 depends on this task. It adds the host installAgents stream, an end-to-end row through this mode, and the readiness probe.

Contract:
- Input frames arrive on stdin and are read the way materialize reads them (snapshot_frames, MAX_HOST_FRAME_BYTES):
  - per binary, one {kind:'agent', cli, size, sha256} header, then its {kind:'data', data} base64 frames;
  - then one {kind:'end'}.
- On success it writes one {kind:'installed', count} frame and exits 0.
- /opt/moe/agents is created if missing and forced to root 0755 through an O_NOFOLLOW directory fd.
- Each binary is written to a 0600 file, opened O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW inside a root 0700 staging directory beside the targets. Its size and sha256 must match its header. It is then made root:root 0555 and fsynced.
- Only after the end frame, with no frame after it, is every binary renamed onto /opt/moe/agents/<cli>, atomically replacing an older install. The directory is then fsynced.
- Exit codes:
  - 65: an unknown cli (not a JOBS key; the type is checked first), a duplicate cli, a size outside 1..MAX_AGENT_BYTES (2^30, mirroring agent-cache.mjs MAX_AGENT_BINARY_BYTES), or a sha256 that is not 64 lowercase hex;
  - 65: a malformed, empty, non-canonical or overlong data frame, a size or hash mismatch, an empty stream, EOF before end, or any frame after end;
  - 74: an I/O failure, including an agents path that is a symlink or a file;
  - 77: not root;
  - 64: any other argv.
- No refusal writes a frame. A handled refusal installs nothing and leaves no staging directory. A crash can leave only the root-only staging directory.

Out of scope:
- the host stream and readiness (CQ-R10d3);
- the JOBS argv and MCP config (CQ-R10d4);
- the cache (CQ-R10d2, done);
- any verified-local or isolation claim.

Verification command (fresh, exit 0 required): node --test scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs. On WSL, run it with env -i HOME="$HOME" PATH="$HOME/.nvm/versions/node/v24.21.0/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin".

implementationPlan.description:
TESTS FIRST (red), scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs. Load test-driven-development.

Append a new section at the end of the file:
`// CQ-R10d3a agents install rows: the real supervisor's install_agents() into <dir>/agents, owned by the test user (the owner seam).`
Reuse PY_LOAD, PY_SUPERVISOR, NOT_POSIX, framesOf, modeOf, scratch, encodeFrame and createFrameDecoder. Every row gets `{ skip: NOT_POSIX }`. ESM import bindings are file-global, so import only names the file does not import yet (e.g. linkSync); a second import of the same name is a SyntaxError. Size budget: about 140 test lines (see planningNotes).

Helper agentsIn(dir, input, setup = '', ...extra), modelled on materializeIn:
- run `${PY_LOAD}${setup}\nsys.exit(m.install_agents(0, 1, sys.argv[2], (os.getuid(), os.getgid())))` under python3 -I -B;
- argv[2] is path.join(dir, 'agents'); pass input, maxBuffer and timeout as M rows do;
- frame builders: agent(cli, bytes) = {kind:'agent', cli, size: bytes.length, sha256: sha256 hex}; data(chunk) = {kind:'data', data: base64}; END = {kind:'end'};
- a state(dir) helper lists <dir>/agents as sorted [name, bytes-or-'dir', mode] rows.

Rows (AI is an unused prefix):

AI1: CLI routing and pins.
- ['agents','x'] and ['AGENTS'] exit 64 with no stdout.
- main(['agents'], geteuid=lambda: 1000) exits 77.
- As root, with install_agents replaced by a stderr-repr lambda, the result is [42, '((0, 1), {})', 0], copying the VR6 pattern.
- The Python constants: m.AGENTS == '/opt/moe/agents'; os.path.dirname of every JOBS executable == m.AGENTS; m.MAX_AGENT_BYTES equals MAX_AGENT_BINARY_BYTES imported from ../local-runner/agent-cache.mjs; inspect.signature(m.install_agents) defaults agents=m.AGENTS and owner=(0, 0).

AI2: a clean install.
- Stream claude (SNAPSHOT_CHUNK_BYTES + 3 bytes, in two data frames) and codex (a few bytes) into a dir with no agents yet.
- Exit 0, and stdout decodes to exactly [{kind:'installed', count:2}].
- agents/claude and agents/codex hold exactly the streamed bytes, mode 0o555, uid = process.getuid().
- The agents dir is mode 0o755, and its listing is exactly ['claude','codex'], with no staging left.

AI3: an older install is replaced, never overwritten in place.
- Pre-create agents (mode 0o777), holding an old claude, plus a hard link to that old file outside agents.
- Install a new claude: agents/claude has the new bytes at 0o555, the hard link still has the old bytes, the agents dir is forced to 0o755, and no staging is left.

AI4: each stream breaks exactly one rule, exits 65, writes no stdout and leaves state(dir) equal to its before-value. Pre-create agents with an old claude, so 'installs nothing' is observable. Rows:
- the cli is 'gemini';
- the cli is ['claude'], 7 or null (type checked before the JOBS lookup, so no TypeError);
- a duplicate claude;
- size 0, size MAX+1 or size true;
- sha256 that is uppercase, 63 chars or not a string;
- the right size but a wrong hash;
- short data before end, or a data chunk longer than what is left;
- an empty data frame, non-canonical base64 'QR==', or a non-string data;
- an extra key in the agent header, or in a data frame;
- a data frame before any header;
- a zero-byte stream;
- an end before any agent (this plan defines it as an empty stream);
- EOF before end;
- a second end after end;
- a partial frame after end;
- a valid claude followed by a bad codex (wrong hash).
Also: the valid base stream exits 0, and the same streams with claude and codex in either order exit 0.

AI5: I/O, each with no stdout.
- agents is a symlink to an outside dir: exit 74, and the link and the outside dir are untouched.
- agents is a regular file: exit 74, and the file is unchanged.
- With os.fsync or os.rename injected to raise OSError(5) (M4's setup pattern): exit 74, and state(dir) is unchanged (the old claude intact, no codex, no staging).

RED proof: `node --test --test-name-pattern='^AI[0-9]' scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs` with the env -i PATH from step 3. Every AI row fails on HEAD (no install_agents, and 'agents' is 64). Record it in the step note.

ADVERSARIAL SELF-REVIEW, once, as the final step. Load adversarial-self-review. Read the diff as a host or agent trying to land bytes it should not.

1. Mutants. Apply each to a scratch copy of guest-supervisor.py, loaded by the tests through a temporary PY_SUPERVISOR override in a scratch copy of the test file; never edit the shared files. Each must turn the named row red:
   (a) skip the sha256 compare: AI4 wrong hash;
   (b) a JOBS lookup before the type check: AI4 list cli (a TypeError escapes);
   (c) rename each binary as soon as it is verified, before end: AI4 'valid claude then bad codex';
   (d) open agents without O_NOFOLLOW: AI5 symlink;
   (e) write the target in place instead of renaming: AI3 hard link;
   (f) default owner AGENT_IDENTITY, or mode 0o755 for binaries: AI1 or AI2;
   (g) accept an end with no agents: AI4 end-first;
   (h) drop the duplicate check: AI4 duplicate (it would exit 74 through O_EXCL);
   (i) no cleanup on refusal: AI4 state (staging left).
   Afterwards restore, cmp, and rerun green.
2. Fds: every fd is closed on every path; no path-based call follows a name the agent could swap; staging is never created outside agents.
3. Bounds: no unbounded read (frames are capped by MAX_HOST_FRAME_BYTES, binaries by MAX_AGENT_BYTES, and the agent count by JOBS).
4. Concurrency: a concurrent second install. Each run gets its own staging name, and renames are per-file atomic, so the last writer wins whole files. Callers serialize per VM (R06 job lease).
5. Scope: no host stream, readiness or argv changes (those belong to CQ-R10d3/R10d4).

Record the findings and fixes in the step note.
